WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.035
-Bernie Sanders won

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:03.535
the New Hampshire primary,
making him

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:05.972
the clear front-runner
for the Democratic nomination,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.641
as President Trump bullied
the Justice Department

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.310
into going easy on one
of his convicted henchmen.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.446
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:17.884 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:20.820
There were two huge developments
happening simultaneously

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.489
on split screens last night:
On the one hand,

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.090
a crisis in the
Justice Department

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.227
created by President Trump;
and, on the other,

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.895
the Democratic primary
in New Hampshire;

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:31.731
and we all had to do our best
to follow both at the same time,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.566
which is just how
our lives are now.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:35.268
We're like bank security guards

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.070
watching five different
screens at once.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.872
[ Laughter ]
On one screen, there's a bunch
of customers waiting patiently

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.807
in line to complain about how
they're bein' ripped off

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:44.376
and, on the other four,
there are dudes staring directly

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:46.979
into the camera, smiling
and holding giant bags of cash.

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:48.581
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.217
First, Democrats held
their second contest

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:53.319
of the primary season
in New Hampshire last night

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:55.255
and, whatever else
you could say about it,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.356
it was honestly
just a relief to move on

00:00:57.356 --> 00:00:59.658
from the mess in Iowa,
where the final results

00:00:59.658 --> 00:01:03.229
were screwed up by mathematical
errors and an app that crashed

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.964
that was made by a company
called Shadow.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.766
[ Laughter ]
In fact, the final results

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.000
are still not confirmed.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.002
A hundred years from now,
after hordes of zombies

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:12.671
supercharged by climate change
have ravaged the country,

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:16.142
[ Laughter ]
a lone survivor will wander
into an abandoned barn in Iowa

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:18.677
and find a note carved
into the wall that says,

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:19.778
"Still too close to call."

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:21.214
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:24.016
Honestly, it was just a relief
to finally see people voting

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.752
in actual polling stations,
as opposed to whatever the hell

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.654
was goin' on in Iowa.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.022
I'm sorry, but this is
not an election.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:31.791
These people look like
the burnout kids

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.092
who had to sit out of volleyball

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:35.562
because they purposely
forgot their gym clothes.

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:36.996
[ Laughter and applause ]
"Sorry, Coach.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:40.232
We're so bummed we can't learn
how to bump, set, and spike!

00:01:40.232 --> 00:01:42.501
[ Laughter and applause ]
The only thing we spike

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:43.802
is heroin, Coach!

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:46.872
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:49.108
[laughing] I'm sorry
I yelled at you, Coach."

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.910
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.479
[laughing] Basically,
what we know about Iowa is

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.648
that Bernie Sanders
won the popular vote;

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.317
Pete Buttigieg slightly
edged him out in the delegates,

00:01:58.317 --> 00:01:59.852
thanks to obscure rules;

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.120
and Elizabeth Warren
came in third.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.823
And the Iowa Democratic Party
is having trouble

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.124
keeping things together.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:07.393
In some cases,
together literally.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:09.695
The chair of the Iowa Party held
a press conference on Monday

00:02:09.695 --> 00:02:12.198
to update the media on the
results, and this happened.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.867
-The sheets are signed,
not only by the precinct chair

00:02:14.867 --> 00:02:15.935
and the precinct secretary --

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.704
[ Clattering ]
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.438
Uh.
-Oh, man.

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:22.575
Did you use an app
for your podium, as well?

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.910
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.645
Was the app called Metaphor?

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:27.913
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:28.947
You can tell.

00:02:28.947 --> 00:02:30.583
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.585
You can tell

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.421
that we had moved on from Iowa
to New Hampshire

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:38.157
because it seemed like
virtually every candidate

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.659
showed up to greet
their supporters

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.428
with the local delicacy boxes
of Dunkin' Donuts,

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.530
[ Laughter ]
and that includes
Senator Amy Klobuchar,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.932
who repeatedly bragged

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:48.234
about how many Dunkin'
locations she'd been to.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.236
-What are you gonna do
to solidify your place

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:53.506
in the top three?

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.441
-Well, Joy, we're doing it
right now.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.743
I go everywhere.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.377
I've been in Dunkin' Donuts.

00:02:58.377 --> 00:02:59.778
I've gone
to Dunkin' Donuts.

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:03.549
And it feels like, for me,
that it's a fresh start here.

00:03:03.549 --> 00:03:06.285
I got to go to every
Dunkin' Donut I could find.

00:03:06.285 --> 00:03:07.921
[ Laughter ]
-That's no small feat.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:10.556
I'm from New Hampshire
and, as I recall,

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.325
every third building
is legally required

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.593
to contain a Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.494
[ Laughter ]
-Whoo!
-Although, I have to say,

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.397
when your big highlight
about visiting New Hampshire is

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:19.065
that you got to go
to every Dunkin' Donut,

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:20.933
you definitely sound like
an out-of-towner.

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:22.668
That's like goin'
to New York and saying,

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.770
"We really got
to experience the culture.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.872
We went to all
the Duane Reeds!"

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:30.009
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.711
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.446
But, hey,

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.815
the strategy clearly worked
for Klobuchar

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:39.885
because she finished in a strong
third, with 20% of the vote.

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:42.121
And, while Andrew Yang
dropping out means

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.356
the remaining Democratic
field is all-white,

00:03:44.356 --> 00:03:46.960
it's pretty amazing that the top
three finishers in New Hampshire

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.927
were a Jewish
Democratic socialist,

00:03:48.927 --> 00:03:51.163
a gay veteran,
and a woman from Minnesota

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.131
whose next coffee
is probably free.

00:03:53.131 --> 00:03:55.268
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:56.903
But the big takeaway --

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:58.237
[ Applause ]

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.673
The big takeaway, of course,
was that Bernie Sanders

00:04:00.673 --> 00:04:02.808
is now the clear front-runner
for the Democratic nomination

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:04.276
with his win in New Hampshire

00:04:04.276 --> 00:04:06.345
and his current lead
in many national polls.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:09.114
And you can tell that he senses
his place as a front-runner

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:11.717
because, in New Hampshire,
he started to aiming his fire

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.652
squarely at Donald Trump.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:18.190
-We are going to defeat
the most dangerous president

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.993
in the modern history
of America: Donald Trump.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.862
[ Cheering ]
The American people,

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:26.599
no matter what their
political views may be,

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.468
are sick and tired

00:04:28.468 --> 00:04:32.838
of a president who is
a pathological liar.

00:04:32.838 --> 00:04:36.509
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:40.679
Who is running
a corrupt administration.

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.848
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:46.885
Who is a bully
and a vindictive person.

00:04:46.885 --> 00:04:48.554
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.924
Who is a racist,

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:54.127
a sexist,

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:56.462
a xenophobe,

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:59.031
a homophobe,

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.900
and a religious bigot.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.602
[ Cheering and applause
intensifies ]

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.972
And those are
his nice qualities.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.674
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:08.808
-Damn!

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:12.144
[ Applause ]
I mean, I gotta say.

00:05:12.144 --> 00:05:13.779
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:16.882
I was always a fan
of Gruff Bernie,

00:05:16.882 --> 00:05:19.285
but I like Insult Comic Bernie
even more.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.653
[ Laughter and applause ]
You can catch that and more

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:24.256
on his new Netflix special,
"Ya Burnt!"

00:05:24.256 --> 00:05:26.291
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:26.291 --> 00:05:29.595
And Trump's actions
this week have shown

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.230
that the stakes
of the Democratic race

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.564
could not be higher.

00:05:32.564 --> 00:05:34.967
Now, the Republicans, with the
exception of Mitt Romney,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.969
have acquitted Trump
in the impeachment trial,

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.405
the 2020 election is really
the last chance we have

00:05:39.405 --> 00:05:41.340
to stop our system
from fully sliding

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.575
into a corrupt banana republic.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.777
Republicans have given Trump
the green light

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.712
to subvert our democracy
and the rule of law

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:49.615
without consequences and, now,
he's pushing full steam ahead.

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.818
He's literally bullying the
Justice Department, via tweet,

00:05:52.818 --> 00:05:54.453
to dole out lenient sentences

00:05:54.453 --> 00:05:56.188
to the cronies who committed
crimes on his behalf.

00:05:56.188 --> 00:05:57.790
Every time I think Trump

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.126
has done the worst thing
he could possibly do,

00:06:00.126 --> 00:06:01.760
he finds a way
to one-up himself.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:03.996
He's like the exact opposite
of Simone Biles.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:07.199
[ Laughter ]
Like every time you think she
can't stun you of a new routine,

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.836
she posts a video of herself
doin' something like this.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.270
-Whoo!

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.271
-Up! Yeah.

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.240
[ Audience oohs ]
-I mean, it's fun

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.176
to imagine Trump attempting
even one part of that routine.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.844
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:21.447
You know, I imagine
it would look like this...

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.515
-Witch hunt.

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:25.217
[ Explosion ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:25.217 --> 00:06:32.859
[ Applause and cheering ]

00:06:32.859 --> 00:06:34.827
-We had like 15 people
workin' all day on that.

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:39.865
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:40.866
[ Laughs ]

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:42.935
[ Fresh laughter ]

00:06:42.935 --> 00:06:44.336
100% first time I've seen it.

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:45.671
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:47.740
Republican Senators tried
to tell us that impeachment

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.942
would be a teachable
moment for Trump,

00:06:49.942 --> 00:06:51.877
but Trump made it clear
that wasn't the case.

00:06:51.877 --> 00:06:54.280
He was basically an inmate
at a parole hearing

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.848
and, when they asked him,
"So, what are your plans

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:56.949
when you get out?"
He said...

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:59.118
[as Trump] Uh,
I'd like to kill again.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.921
[ Laughter ]
Last night, we saw how little
Trump has changed

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.956
with the case of one
of his long-time confidants,

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.390
convicted criminal Roger Stone,

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:08.694
seen here in his very real
outfit from the inauguration.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:09.695
[ Laughter ]
I mean, look at him.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:11.096
Is he attending the inauguration

00:07:11.096 --> 00:07:12.531
or Mr. Peanut's funeral?

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.433
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:16.802
He's dressed like
Punxsutawney Phil's coke dealer.

00:07:16.802 --> 00:07:18.504
"Good news, Phil, baby.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:21.406
Six more weeks of winter
and it's the good snow, baby."

00:07:21.406 --> 00:07:22.908
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:23.909
[laughing] Stone --

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:26.645
[ Applause ]
-Whoo!

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:29.048
-Stone was convicted
of lying to Congress

00:07:29.048 --> 00:07:31.917
and witness tampering, both
actions intended to help Trump

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:33.752
during Robert Mueller's
Russia investigation.

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:35.388
You might remember that Stone

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:37.289
even tried to intimidate
one witness

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:40.792
by threatening to steal
that witness' therapy dog.

00:07:40.792 --> 00:07:43.262
Stone wrote in an email,
"You are a rat. A stoolie.

00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:45.197
You backstab your friends--
run your mouth

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:47.566
my lawyers are dying
to Rip you to shreds."

00:07:47.566 --> 00:07:50.469
Stone also said he would
"take that dog away from you."

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.139
[ Laughter ]
That's right. He threatened
to take someone's therapy dog.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:55.674
Even Spirit Airlines
doesn't do that.

00:07:55.674 --> 00:07:58.244
[ Laughter ]
And they don't even
have cushions.

00:07:58.244 --> 00:07:59.512
[ Laughter ]

00:07:59.512 --> 00:08:01.414
So, on Monday,
prosecutors recommended

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:02.948
up to nine years
in jail for Stone

00:08:02.948 --> 00:08:04.249
and then,
in the middle of the night,

00:08:04.249 --> 00:08:06.785
Trump lashed out at that
sentence on Twitter, writing,

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:08.854
"This is a horrible
and very unfair situation.

00:08:08.854 --> 00:08:10.223
The real crimes are
on the other side,

00:08:10.223 --> 00:08:11.423
as nothing happens to them.

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:13.225
Cannot allow this
miscarriage of justice."

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:15.794
He lied to Congress,
tampered with witnesses,

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:17.563
and threatened
to steal someone's dog.

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.431
Dognapping, alone,
should get you jail time

00:08:19.431 --> 00:08:22.001
and you should have to serve
those years in a dog pound.

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.536
[ Laughter and applause ]
And then, outta nowhere,

00:08:24.536 --> 00:08:26.072
in a shocking move,
the Justice Department,

00:08:26.072 --> 00:08:29.041
led by Trump's co-conspirator,
Attorney General Bill Barr,

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.909
announced on Tuesday
they were changing

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:33.178
the sentencing recommendation,
after Trump's tweet,

00:08:33.178 --> 00:08:35.948
prompting all four prosecutors
working on the case

00:08:35.948 --> 00:08:37.516
to withdraw in protest.

00:08:37.516 --> 00:08:38.784
Barr is turning
the Justice Department

00:08:38.784 --> 00:08:40.119
into a political weapon
for Trump

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:42.788
and, when Trump was asked
about the move yesterday,

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.190
he insisted both that he hadn't
directed the Justice Department

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:46.725
to go easy on Stone and also,

00:08:46.725 --> 00:08:50.329
that he had the absolute right
to do it, if he had wanted to.

00:08:50.329 --> 00:08:51.563
-You seemed,
from your tweet today,

00:08:51.563 --> 00:08:54.333
that were upset about the
Roger Stone sentencing.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.901
-Yeah.
I thought it was ridiculous.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:57.536
-Did you ask the Justice --
-No, I didn't speak

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.571
to the Justice -- I'd be able
to do it, if I wanted.

00:08:59.571 --> 00:09:01.306
I have the absolute right
to do it.

00:09:01.306 --> 00:09:03.909
I stay out of things,

00:09:03.909 --> 00:09:05.544
to a degree that people
wouldn't believe.

00:09:05.544 --> 00:09:07.179
[ Laughter ]
-No. We wouldn't.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:08.180
We wouldn't believe it.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.948
You don't stay out of anything.

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:11.851
You couldn't even stay
out of Robert Pattinson's

00:09:11.851 --> 00:09:13.418
and Kristen Stewart's
relationship.

00:09:13.418 --> 00:09:15.053
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:15.053 --> 00:09:18.423
You're like the guy at a party
who walks up to a couple

00:09:18.423 --> 00:09:20.025
that are clearly fighting
and says...

00:09:20.025 --> 00:09:21.494
[as Trump]
So, who cheated on who?

00:09:21.494 --> 00:09:22.528
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:24.463
Karen! I didn't know
you had it in ya.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:26.865
[ Laughter ]
Also, this is not the first time

00:09:26.865 --> 00:09:28.567
Trump has insisted
he has the absolute right

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:29.868
to direct
the Justice Department

00:09:29.868 --> 00:09:32.471
to do his political bidding
or, the absolute right

00:09:32.471 --> 00:09:35.173
to do a buncha other obviously
unconstitutional stuff.

00:09:35.173 --> 00:09:37.443
-He tweeted, "As the President
of the United States,

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:40.112
I have an absolute right,
perhaps even a duty,

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:43.015
to investigate, or have
investigated, CORRUPTION,

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.584
and that would include
asking or suggesting

00:09:45.584 --> 00:09:47.319
other Countries to help us out!"

00:09:47.319 --> 00:09:49.855
-"I never offered Pardons
to Homeland Security Officials,

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:51.724
never ordered anyone
to close our Southern border

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:54.526
